## Differential

For

```text
F1 = R(-11)^4 + R(-14)^15 + R(-15)^11,
F2 = R(-12) + R(-13) + R(-16)^40 + R(-17)^7,
```

the theorem constructs

```text
d2:F2 -> F1.
```

Its 49 minimal columns occur exactly as

```text
1 column  in total degree 12,
1 column  in total degree 13,
40 columns in total degree 16,
7 columns  in total degree 17.
```

At each degree the construction computes `ker(d1)`, quotients by all variable
multiples of the preceding kernel, eliminates the inherited pivot rows and
normalizes the quotient pivot rows to the identity. The same chart works at
all eight primes and six roots per prime.

The resulting columns satisfy

```text
d1*d2=0
```

literally, and their monomial multiples equal `ker(d1)` through degree 18.

